{"title":"Topicwise Test-20 Part Syllabus GATE 2025 CS Digital Logic-2","fileName":"073_Topicwise Test-20 Part Syllabus GATE 2025 CS Digital Logic-2.html","branch":"COMPUTER SCIENCE ENGINEERING","series":"GATE 2026 GATE 2025 Online Test Series Computer Science Engineering","provider":"MADE EASY","duration":2700,"questions":[{"qnum":1,"type":"MCQ","correct":"B","right":1,"wrong":0.33,"qtext":"<p>A <em>PN</em> flip-flop has following four operations:</p>\n<p><img src=\"/media/7f3ed0afdd12466b58a89b60471077768c0615f1.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>\n<p>The characteristic equation of the above flip-flop is</p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div> <p>\n <em>PQ</em> + <em>NQ</em>′</p></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"B","text":"<div> <p>\n <em>PQ</em>′ + <em>NQ</em></p></div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"C","text":"<div> <p>\n <em>P</em>′<em>Q</em> + <em>NQ</em>′</p></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"D","text":"<div> <p>\n <em>P</em>′<em>Q</em>′ + <em>NQ</em></p></div>","isCorrect":false}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p>(b)</p>\n<p><img src=\"/media/65326fdac386176266217e4722b23dcc5b9477b2.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":2,"type":"MCQ","correct":"C","right":1,"wrong":0.33,"qtext":"<p>Consider the diagram shown below:</p>\n<p><img src=\"/media/52ed1af184be617efd8d4c8aff5d0f4c69938a36.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>\n<p>The above diagram perform the operation of</p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div> <p>\n <em>D</em> flip-flop</p></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"B","text":"<div> <p>\n <em>T</em> flip-flop</p></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"C","text":"<div> <p>\n <em>JK</em> flip-flop</p></div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"D","text":"<div> <p>\n <em>SR</em> flip-flop</p></div>","isCorrect":false}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p>(c)</p>\n<p><img src=\"/media/930e22dd1e4879b6084dd9678bf41f19439e2b00.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":3,"type":"MCQ","correct":"C","right":1,"wrong":0.33,"qtext":"<p>The characteristic equation for the complement output of a JK flip-flop is</p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div> <p>\n <img src=\"/media/d0f20ae47ba1d82a0030eeaf3262a76fda8bd7a4.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"B","text":"<div> <p>\n <img src=\"/media/778e8500fa629fa7a1dcf748bb0e5bd97b8a4f32.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"C","text":"<div> <p>\n <img src=\"/media/945e343d7847e7ed68ca79c9ff11589073fcc6b5.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p></div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"D","text":"<div> <p>\n <img src=\"/media/71a1ba6fa9d23260dd1fe33a3c6607f6a5ca68d6.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p></div>","isCorrect":false}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p>(c)</p>\n<p><img src=\"/media/16d3b54da7a939ea4f9043d4cb7422f2983b6900.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":4,"type":"NAT","correct":"","right":1,"wrong":0,"qtext":"<p>The duty cycle of the most significant bit form a 4 bit BCD counter is ____ (in %).</p></div>\n<div><span>NAT</span>","options":[],"nat":{"low":"20","high":"20"},"solution":"<p>20</p>\n<p><img src=\"/media/ab79efe8e8b995997d97a2ae3f937ca7ecf13f1f.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":5,"type":"MCQ","correct":"B","right":1,"wrong":0.33,"qtext":"<p>To count a decimal number sequence from 0 to 512, we wish to design a counter. For this counter the number of flip-flops required are</p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div> 9</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"B","text":"<div> 10</div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"C","text":"<div> 11</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"D","text":"<div> 8</div>","isCorrect":false}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p>(b)<br />\nFrom 0 to (511)<sub>10</sub> total number of decimal numbers are 512, so for this count we require (29 = 512) 9 flip-flops.<br />\nHence, 9 + 1 = 10 flip-flops are required to count from 0 to 512.</p>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":6,"type":"NAT","correct":"","right":1,"wrong":0,"qtext":"<p>A 4-bit MOD-6 ripple counter uses J-K flip-flops. If propagation delay of each flip-flop is 20 nsec, then the maximum clock frequency used is ________ MHz.</p></div>\n<div><span>NAT</span>","options":[],"nat":{"low":"12.5","high":"12.5"},"solution":"<p>12.5</p>\n<p><img src=\"/media/d7b5b332e719dde432162b29acd7d0cae01cd944.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":7,"type":"MSQ","correct":"A,B,C","right":2,"wrong":0,"qtext":"<p>Which of the following statements is/are correct regarding Master Slave JK flip flop?</p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div> Master flip-flop responds to positive edge of clock.</div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"B","text":"<div> Slave flip-flop responds to negative edge of clock.</div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"C","text":"<div> It helps in avoiding the race around condition in JK flip flop</div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"D","text":"<div> Output change only during positive edge transition of the clock.</div>","isCorrect":false}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p>(a, b, c)<br />\nOutput of Master Slave JK flip flop change only during negative edge transition of the clock.</p>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":8,"type":"MSQ","correct":"A,B,D","right":2,"wrong":0,"qtext":"<p>Consider the following logic diagram:</p>\n<p><img src=\"/media/334af1fe781011613ce919e842a03756fc2979bf.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>\n<p>After a clock pulse which values of <em>ABC</em> will generate output Z as logic 0. Assume before applying <em>ABC</em> inputs the flip-flops are cleared.</p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div> 111</div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"B","text":"<div> 101</div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"C","text":"<div> 001</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"D","text":"<div> 110</div>","isCorrect":true}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p>(a, b, d)</p>\n<p><img src=\"/media/4c2161474831cf30abdd1f9ce2b3deac1a6aea27.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":9,"type":"MSQ","correct":"B,C","right":1,"wrong":0,"qtext":"<p>In the latch circuit shown, the NAND gates have non-zero, but unequal propagation delay. The present input condition is ; <em>P</em> = <em>Q</em> = ‘0’. If the input condition is changed simultaneously to <em>P</em> = <em>Q</em> = ‘1’, the outputs <em>X</em> and <em>Y</em> are</p>\n<p><img src=\"/media/60dab9936c2e2385b1811eab3d323a8d429132fd.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div> <p>\n <img src=\"/media/5b8f67039cc20dbf128cbfb99244b3fc443b15de.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"B","text":"<div> <p>\n <img src=\"/media/b8e4d9d618fb8c0516a0253ade403fc66b73067a.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p></div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"C","text":"<div> <p>\n <img src=\"/media/144289a5f62c1ea9e76a990dcfbdb518d45de58a.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p></div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"D","text":"<div> <p>\n <img src=\"/media/7a513c6548335bd56865bf86061d3e60963b892a.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p></div>","isCorrect":false}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p>(b, c)</p>\n<p><img src=\"/media/483cf7f0f8fcb2ded7a1a698e6de97b1e30bfa4b.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":10,"type":"MCQ","correct":"B","right":1,"wrong":0.33,"qtext":"<p>Three shift registers are initialized and are connected as shown below, having a common clock.<br />\nThen the contents of register-A after 10 clock pulses is</p>\n<p><img src=\"/media/e679de7441e24e3a07780269252dc852f7755deb.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div> 1011</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"B","text":"<div> 0101</div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"C","text":"<div> 1001</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"D","text":"<div> 0110</div>","isCorrect":false}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p>(b)</p>\n<p><img src=\"/media/30277ac4d06eeb5b99da706956db1577aba7ddf0.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":11,"type":"MCQ","c